=encoding utf8

=head1 NAME

std/time - Time objects, formatting, and parsing.

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  from std/time import Time, TimeParser;

  let now := new Time();
  let t0  := new Time(0);

  let parser := new TimeParser("%Y-%m-%d");
  let d := parser.parse("2026-03-20");

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This module provides C<Time> for working with timestamps and
C<TimeParser> for parsing strings using a strptime format.

=head2 Classes

=over

=item C<< Time(Number epoch?) >>

Construct a time from an epoch value in seconds, or use the current
local time when omitted.

Common instance methods include:

=over

=item * Components

C<sec>, C<min>, C<hour>, C<day_of_month>, C<mon>, C<month>,
C<year>, C<yy>, C<day_of_week>, C<day>, C<day_of_year>,
C<month_last_day>, C<epoch>.

=item * Formatting

C<hms>, C<ymd>, C<mdy>, C<dmy>, C<date>, C<time>,
C<datetime>, C<cdate>, C<strftime>, C<to_String>.

=item * Calendar helpers

C<tzoffset>, C<is_leap_year>, C<week>, C<week_year>,
C<julian_day>.

=item * Arithmetic

C<add_seconds>, C<add_minutes>, C<add_hours>, C<add_days>,
C<add_weeks>, and on supported builds C<add_months> and
C<add_years>.

=back

=item C<< TimeParser(String format = "%Y-%m-%d") >>

Create a parser for the given format string.

=item C<< TimeParser->parse(String text) >>

Parse text and return a C<Time> object.

=back

